-- title:
--   Frobenius kernel has order p^{dim_k ω}
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field of characteristic $p$, where $p$ is prime, and let $H$ be a commutative ring carrying the structure of a Hopf algebra over $k$ which is finite-dimensional as a $k$-module. Write $\varepsilon =$ `Bialgebra.counitAlgHom k H` for the counit, viewed as a $k$-algebra homomorphism $H \to k$, and let $I = \ker \varepsilon$ be its kernel, the augmentation ideal. Let $J \subseteq H$ be the ideal generated by the image of $I$ under the $p$-th power map, i.e. by the set $\{a^p : a \in I\}$. The assertion is the equality of $k$-dimensions
--   $$\dim_k (H/J) = p^{\dim_k (I/I^2)},$$
--   where the exponent is the $k$-dimension of `Ideal.Cotangent` of $I$, that is of $I/I^2$. In the language of schemes, with $G = \operatorname{Spec} H$ the finite commutative group scheme attached to $H$, this says that the closed subscheme cut out by $p$-th powers of augmentation elements — the kernel of the relative Frobenius — has order $p^{\dim_k \omega_G}$, $\omega_G = I/I^2$ being the cotangent space of $G$ at the identity.
--
--   This is the standard order computation for the Frobenius kernel of a finite commutative group scheme in characteristic $p$, a consequence of Cartier's structure theorem for finite bialgebras of height one; it is obtained here from [`HopfAlgebra.finrank_eq_pow_finrank_cotangent_of_forall_pow_prime_eq_zero`](thm.html#HopfAlgebra.finrank_eq_pow_finrank_cotangent_of_forall_pow_prime_eq_zero), which treats a finite $k$-bialgebra in which every element of the augmentation kernel has vanishing $p$-th power. It feeds the structure theory of finite flat group schemes used in the project, being cited for the presentation of such Hopf algebras as truncated polynomial rings, for cocycle computations, and for the recognition of Frobenius kernels in the Cherednik–Drinfeld setting.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_HopfAlgebra_finrank_quotient_span_pow_prime_eq_pow_finrank_cotangent.lean

